    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p39-q34-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that\n$$a^2+b^2+c^2=2bc\\cos A+2ac\\cos B+2ab\\cos C.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p39-q34-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "a^2+b^2+c^2=2bc\\cos A+2ac\\cos B+2ab\\cos C",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p39-q34-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the three cosine-rule equations and rearrange.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The three cosine-rule equations are\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2&=b^2+c^2-2bc\\cos A\\\\b^2&=a^2+c^2-2ac\\cos B\\\\c^2&=a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos C.\\end{align*}$$\nAdd the equations. The squared-side terms on the right total $2(a^2+b^2+c^2)$. Rearranging gives\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2+b^2+c^2&=2bc\\cos A+2ac\\cos B+2ab\\cos C.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q34-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $ab=\\dfrac{2T}{\\sin C}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p39-q34-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "ab=\\frac{2T}{\\sin C}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p39-q34-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rearrange the triangle area rule.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "By the area rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}T&=\\frac12ab\\sin C\\\\ab&=\\frac{2T}{\\sin C}.\\end{align*}$$\nDivision is valid because $0^\\circ<C<180^\\circ$, so $\\sin C>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q34-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p39-q34-c-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Hence, show that",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p39-q34-c-formula",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "center",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "T=\\frac14\\times\\left(\\frac{a^2+b^2+c^2}{\\cot A+\\cot B+\\cot C}\\right)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p39-q34-cot-definition",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Note:",
                  "marks": [
                    "italic"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\cot\\theta=\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ". More on this in the next chapter.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p39-q34-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "T=\\frac{a^2+b^2+c^2}{4(\\cot A+\\cot B+\\cot C)}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p39-q34-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Substitute the three area-rule rearrangements into part (a), use the cotangent definition and solve for ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "T",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "As in part (b),\n$$\\begin{align*}ac&=\\frac{2T}{\\sin B}\\\\bc&=\\frac{2T}{\\sin A}.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute these and $ab=\\dfrac{2T}{\\sin C}$ into part (a):\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2+b^2+c^2&=4T\\left(\\frac{\\cos A}{\\sin A}+\\frac{\\cos B}{\\sin B}+\\frac{\\cos C}{\\sin C}\\right)\\\\a^2+b^2+c^2&=4T(\\cot A+\\cot B+\\cot C)\\\\T&=\\frac14\\times\\left(\\frac{a^2+b^2+c^2}{\\cot A+\\cot B+\\cot C}\\right).\\end{align*}$$\nThe denominator is positive, since $\\cot A+\\cot B+\\cot C=\\dfrac{a^2+b^2+c^2}{4T}>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q34-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Use this formula to find the area of an equilateral triangle of side length $s$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p39-q34-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "T=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}s^2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p39-q34-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "a=b=c=s",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\cot60^\\circ=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " in part (c).",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For an equilateral triangle, $a=b=c=s$ and $A=B=C=60^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cot60^\\circ&=\\frac{\\frac12}{\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}}\\\\\\cot60^\\circ&=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the formula in part (c),\n$$\\begin{align*}T&=\\frac14\\times\\frac{3s^2}{3/\\sqrt3}\\\\T&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}s^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
